 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_1d5b131115789f13c422f042db140fa1" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_65aeba2845139a812f18688b2b554c52" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FAD synthase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q8NFF5" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_FLAD1_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FAD1_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Molybdenum cofactor biosynthesis protein-like region</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FLAD1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FAD synthase region</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.7.2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FMN adenylyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Flavin adenine dinucleotide synthase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FAD pyrophosphorylase</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FAD1_HUMAN Reviewed; 587 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot.isoform/Q8NFF5-2</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the adenylation of flavin mononucleotide (FMN)to form flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD) coenzyme.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:16643857, ECO:0000269|PubMed:27259049}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=ATP + FMN + H(+) = diphosphate + FAD;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:17237, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:30616,ChEBI:CHEBI:33019, ChEBI:CHEBI:57692, ChEBI:CHEBI:58210;EC=2.7.7.2; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:16643857};COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:16643857,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17049878};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=1.5 uM for FMN {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16643857,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17049878};KM=0.36 uM for FMN (isoform 2) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16643857,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17049878};Vmax=6.1 nmol/min/mg enzyme {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16643857,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17049878};Vmax=3.9 nmol/min/mg enzyme (isoform 2){ECO:0000269|PubMed:16643857, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17049878};PATHWAY: Cofactor biosynthesis; FAD biosynthesis; FAD from FMN:step 1/1.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform 1: Mitochondrion matrix{ECO:0000269|PubMed:20060505}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform 2: Cytoplasm.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=5;Name=1; Synonyms=FADS1 {ECO:0000303|PubMed:27259049};IsoId=Q8NFF5-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2; Synonyms=FADS2 {ECO:0000303|PubMed:27259049};IsoId=Q8NFF5-2; Sequence=VSP_027947;Name=3;IsoId=Q8NFF5-3; Sequence=VSP_027947, VSP_027954;Name=4;IsoId=Q8NFF5-4; Sequence=VSP_027948, VSP_027949, VSP_027951,VSP_027952;Name=5;IsoId=Q8NFF5-5; Sequence=VSP_027948, VSP_027949, VSP_027950,VSP_027953;DOMAIN: The molybdenum cofactor biosynthesis protein-like regionmay not be functional.DISEASE: Lipid storage myopathy due to flavin adenine dinucleotidesynthetase deficiency (LSMFLAD) [MIM:255100]: An autosomalrecessive, inborn error of metabolism characterized by variablemitochondrial dysfunction. Clinical features range from severecardiac and respiratory insufficiency with onset in infancy andresulting in early death, to mild muscle weakness with onset inadulthood. Some patients show significant improvement withriboflavin treatment. Analysis of skeletal muscle show multiplemitochondrial respiratory chain deficiency and a lipid storagemyopathy in most patients. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:27259049}. Note=Thedisease is caused by mutations affecting the gene represented inthis entry.SIMILARITY: In the N-terminal section; belongs to the MoaB/Mogfamily. {ECO:0000305}.SIMILARITY: In the C-terminal section; belongs to the PAPSreductase family. FAD1 subfamily. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
